# Derived by hand from the dynamic law (R2/R3) as ruled for structural dynamics (round 3 ST): with S(n) the snapshot as the last act of n's construction, the dynamic after m is S(m-1); it is published at n+1, the first firing of that owed tick, when S(n) differs from S(n-1), so `!Updated $doc` fires at n+1 with S(n) and a lifted dynamic over it and a hold is an ordinary dynamic, firing in the tick its hold is written with the document one tick behind; R7 (a newborn row is built at the end of its tick) and ch. 9's forwarding (re-emission at host/[p]/0, the host's rows reading the structure itself).
test one_state_in_the_sample_and_the_event

tick 0
  added:
    0/[0]/0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    0/[1/[1]/0]/0: Ui.Label(text="k1")
    1: Ui.Button(label="tap")
    2: Ui.Label(text="0 moves, 2 places")
    3: Ui.Label(text="seen 0 places at 0 clicks")

tick 1
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="seen 2 places at 1 clicks")

tick 2

tick 3
  in:
    0/[0]/0: click
    1: click
  added:
    0/[1/[2]/0]/0: Ui.Label(text="k2")
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="seen 2 places at 2 clicks")

tick 4
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="1 moves, 3 places")
    3: Ui.Label(text="seen 3 places at 2 clicks")

tick 5
  in:
    0/[0]/0: click
  added:
    0/[1/[3]/0]/0: Ui.Label(text="k3")

tick 6
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="2 moves, 4 places")
    3: Ui.Label(text="seen 4 places at 2 clicks")

test a_gathered_dynamic_fires_next_tick

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="one")
    2: Ui.Label(text="0 heard, 0 rows")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    1/[2]/0: Ui.Label(text="three")

tick 2
  changed:
